WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Today we talk about hash tables and why they are fast.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:45.000
A hash function maps a key to a bucket index in an array

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:05.000
When two keys land in the same bucket we call that a collision.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Chaining stores a linked list in each bucket. Lookups walk the list.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:02:10.000
Open addressing probes other buckets instead. Both approaches degrade when the load factor grows.
